# Cursor Rules for Creative Workspace

## General Guidelines
- Always use absolute paths when possible for better reliability
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones unless explicitly requested
- Maintain consistent formatting and structure across all projects
- Respect the creative nature of this workspace and preserve artistic intent

## Code Style & Formatting
- Use clear, descriptive variable and function names
- Add comments for complex logic or creative decisions
- Maintain consistent indentation (prefer spaces over tabs)
- Follow language-specific conventions for each project type

## File Organization
- Keep project-specific files within their respective folders
- Use meaningful folder names that reflect the project content
- Maintain a clear separation between different project types
- Preserve existing folder structure unless explicitly asked to reorganize

## Creative Content Guidelines
- Respect the artistic vision and creative direction
- Maintain consistency in tone, style, and voice within each project
- Preserve character development and narrative flow
- Keep creative elements intact when making technical improvements

## Documentation
- Only create documentation files when explicitly requested
- Use clear, concise language in any technical documentation
- Include relevant context for creative decisions when documenting code

## Error Handling
- Fix linter errors when clear solutions are available
- Don't make uneducated guesses for complex issues
- Ask for clarification when creative decisions are ambiguous
- Preserve original intent when fixing technical issues

## Project-Specific Notes
- This workspace contains multiple creative projects (books, stories, etc.)
- Each project folder should maintain its own structure and conventions
- Core files and working directories serve different purposes within projects
- Templates folder contains reusable components and patterns

## Communication
- Be concise but thorough in explanations
- Focus on practical solutions that enhance creativity
- Respect the creative process and artistic vision
- Provide clear guidance for technical improvements without compromising artistic integrity
